      "writtenOn": "2023-01-12T19:10:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From a code style perspective, it would be much clearer if you had a `CasManifest` interface type with two implementations: a working one and a null one.\n\nThis way your call site becomes:\n\n```\nz.casManifest.append(op)\n```\n\nAnd at the end you just write it out:\n\n```\nerr :\u003d z.casManifest.write()\n```\n\nThe null implementation does nothing.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 585,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 585,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "fc6f9972ae8b6c0e78b79fa4126cdca17b784d09",
